        <!-- Join -->
        <h2 class="fw-bold mt-5">9. join()</h2>

        <p>
            The <code>join()</code> method makes one thread wait until another thread completes.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-4">
            <span class="code-lang-tag">Java</span>
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args)
            throws InterruptedException {

        Thread worker = new Thread(() -&gt; {

            for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) {
                System.out.println("Worker: " + i);
            }
        });

        worker.start();

        worker.join();

        System.out.println("Worker completed");
    }
}</code></pre>
        </div>
