        <!-- Deadlock -->
        <h2 class="fw-bold mt-5">26. Deadlock</h2>

        <p>
            A <strong>deadlock</strong> occurs when two or more threads wait forever for
            resources held by each other.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-4">
            <span class="code-lang-tag">Concept</span>
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>Thread 1:
Lock A → waits for Lock B

Thread 2:
Lock B → waits for Lock A</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-danger">
            <strong>Avoid deadlocks by:</strong>
            keeping lock ordering consistent, minimizing lock scope,
            and avoiding unnecessary nested locks.
        </div>

        <!-- Starvation -->
        <h2 class="fw-bold mt-5">27. Starvation</h2>

        <p>
            <strong>Starvation</strong> occurs when a thread continuously fails to obtain
            the CPU or required resources because other threads keep getting priority.
        </p>

        <!-- Livelock -->
        <h2 class="fw-bold mt-5">28. Livelock</h2>

        <p>
            In a <strong>livelock</strong>, threads are active but continuously respond to
            each other without making useful progress.
        </p>

